<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies nine issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies nine issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said it has qualified for bond insurance the following nine issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Anaheim, Calif., $95 million electric revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--California State University, Calif., $13.130 million revs and $4 million revs.</p>
<p>--Groton Town, Conn., $3.720 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Tinley Park, Ill., $3.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Westford, Mass., $9.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Leonia Board of Education, N.J., $4.99 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Clark County, Nev., $120 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cumberland County S.D., Wis., $8.5 million refunding GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
